{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VVvHRHKgb5uuDEeifcmY1f","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: test-rel02.0\n     2→title: \"Test Suite: rel02.0 — ls core and du specification and differential tests\"\n     3→release: rel02.0\n     4→\n     5→traces:\n     6→  - rel02.0-uc001-ls\n     7→  - rel02.0-uc002-du\n     8→  - prd008-ls R1\n     9→  - prd008-ls R2\n    10→  - prd008-ls R3\n    11→  - prd008-ls R4\n    12→  - prd008-ls R5\n    13→  - prd008-ls R6\n    14→  - prd008-ls R7\n    15→  - prd009-du R1\n    16→  - prd009-du R2\n    17→  - prd009-du R3\n    18→  - prd009-du R4\n    19→  - prd009-du R5\n    20→\n    21→preconditions:\n    22→  - Binaries exist under ./bin/ (built via mage build).\n    23→  - Reference binaries are installed via Homebrew gls (coreutils) and gdu (coreutils).\n    24→  - Tests are run via go test ./cmd/<utility>/... which invokes RunDiffTests from pkg/testutils.\n    25→  - All tests use LC_ALL=C to eliminate locale-dependent divergence.\n    26→  - \"ls: all differential tests use --color=never to eliminate ANSI escape variance (except color-specific structural tests).\"\n    27→  - \"ls: for -l tests, the LsNormalizer replaces the mtime column with the placeholder MTIME before comparison.\"\n    28→  - \"ls: tests use a fixture directory (testdata/ls-fixture/) containing regular files of known sizes, a subdirectory, dotfiles, a symbolic link, and files with known permissions.\"\n    29→  - \"du: no normalization is applied; du output is deterministic when both binaries run on the same directory on the same filesystem.\"\n    30→  - \"du: all block-count tests use -k to pin output to 1024-byte blocks and eliminate platform default divergence.\"\n    31→  - \"du: tests use a fixture directory (testdata/du-fixture/) containing nested files of known sizes, a second subdirectory for multi-argument tests, and files of varied sizes.\"\n    32→  - \"du: hard-link pairs are created in test setup (not committed) to test dedup. All files in the fixture are on the same filesystem as the test runner.\"\n    33→\n    34→test_cases:\n    35→  # --- uc001-ls: ls core flag listing ---\n    36→\n    37→  - name: ls_default_single_col_redirect\n    38→    description: 'No flags, stdout redirected (not a TTY); one entry per line in C locale order. stdout is a pipe (not TTY), so default format is single-column'\n    39→    inputs:\n    40→      args: [\"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n    41→      stdin: null\n    42→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    43→    normalization: none\n    44→    expected:\n    45→      exit_code: 0\n    46→      stdout_structure: one entry per line, sorted in C locale order, no dotfiles\n    47→      stderr: \"\"\n    48→    traces:\n    49→      - prd008-ls R1.2\n    50→      - prd008-ls R1.3\n    51→      - prd008-ls R1.4\n    52→\n    53→  - name: ls_default_multi_col_tty\n    54→    description: 'Default on TTY (or forced with -C and --width=80); multi-column output. -C forces multi-column even without TTY; -w 80 sets column width'\n    55→    inputs:\n    56→      args: [\"-C\", \"--color=never\", \"-w\", \"80\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n    57→      stdin: null\n    58→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    59→    normalization: none\n    60→    expected:\n    61→      exit_code: 0\n    62→      stdout_structure: entries arranged in columns fitting within 80 characters\n    63→      stderr: \"\"\n    64→    traces:\n    65→      - prd008-ls R1.1\n    66→\n    67→  - name: ls_single_col_flag\n    68→    description: -1 forces single-column output regardless of TTY.\n    69→    inputs:\n    70→      args: [\"-1\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n    71→      stdin: null\n    72→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    73→    normalization: none\n    74→    expected:\n    75→      exit_code: 0\n    76→      stdout_structure: one entry per line, sorted in C locale order\n    77→      stderr: \"\"\n    78→    traces:\n    79→      - prd008-ls R2.1\n    80→\n    81→  - name: ls_long_format\n    82→    description: -l produces long format with permissions, nlink, owner, group, size, mtime, name.\n    83→    inputs:\n    84→      args: [\"-l\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n    85→      stdin: null\n    86→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    87→    normalization: LsNormalizer replaces mtime column with MTIME placeholder\n    88→    expected:\n    89→      exit_code: 0\n    90→      stdout_structure: |\n    91→        \"total N\" line followed by one long-format line per entry.\n    92→        Each line has: type+perms, nlink, owner, group, size, MTIME, name.\n    93→      stderr: \"\"\n    94→    traces:\n    95→      - prd008-ls R2.2\n    96→      - prd008-ls R2.3\n    97→      - prd008-ls R2.4\n    98→      - prd008-ls R2.5\n    99→      - prd008-ls R2.6\n   100→      - prd008-ls R2.7\n   101→      - prd008-ls R2.9\n   102→\n   103→  - name: ls_long_format_symlink\n   104→    description: -l on a directory containing a symlink shows \"name -> target\".\n   105→    inputs:\n   106→      args: [\"-l\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n   107→      stdin: null\n   108→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   109→    normalization: LsNormalizer replaces mtime column with MTIME placeholder\n   110→    expected:\n   111→      exit_code: 0\n   112→      stdout_structure: 'output contains \" -> \"'\n   113→      stderr: \"\"\n   114→    traces:\n   115→      - prd008-ls R2.8\n   116→\n   117→  - name: ls_long_human\n   118→    description: -lh displays human-readable file sizes matching gls -lh.\n   119→    inputs:\n   120→      args: [\"-lh\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n   121→      stdin: null\n   122→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   123→    normalization: LsNormalizer replaces mtime column with MTIME placeholder\n   124→    expected:\n   125→      exit_code: 0\n   126→      stdout_structure: long format with sizes like \"1.0K\", \"1.5K\", \"1.0M\" instead of byte counts\n   127→      stderr: \"\"\n   128→    traces:\n   129→      - prd008-ls R5.1\n   130→      - prd008-ls R5.2\n   131→\n   132→  - name: ls_filter_all\n   133→    description: -a includes all entries including . and .. and dotfiles.\n   134→    inputs:\n   135→      args: [\"-a\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n   136→      stdin: null\n   137→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   138→    normalization: none\n   139→    expected:\n   140→      exit_code: 0\n   141→      stdout_structure: 'output contains \".\", \"..\", and \".hidden\"'\n   142→      stderr: \"\"\n   143→    traces:\n   144→      - prd008-ls R3.1\n   145→\n   146→  - name: ls_filter_almost_all\n   147→    description: -A includes dotfiles but excludes . and .. entries.\n   148→    inputs:\n   149→      args: [\"-A\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n   150→      stdin: null\n   151→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   152→    normalization: none\n   153→    expected:\n   154→      exit_code: 0\n   155→      stdout_structure: 'output contains \".hidden\" and must not contain standalone \".\" or \"..\" entries'\n   156→      stderr: \"\"\n   157→    traces:\n   158→      - prd008-ls R3.2\n   159→\n   160→  - name: ls_directory_itself\n   161→    description: -d shows the directory entry itself, not its contents.\n   162→    inputs:\n   163→      args: [\"-d\", \"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n   164→      stdin: null\n   165→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   166→    normalization: none\n   167→    expected:\n   168→      exit_code: 0\n   169→      stdout: \"testdata/ls-fixture/\\n\"\n   170→      stderr: \"\"\n   171→    traces:\n   172→      - prd008-ls R3.3\n   173→\n   174→  - name: ls_color_suppressed\n   175→    description: --color=never produces no ANSI escape sequences.\n   176→    inputs:\n   177→      args: [\"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n   178→      stdin: null\n   179→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   180→    normalization: none\n   181→    expected:\n   182→  