iate children.\n   292→    inputs:\n   293→      args: [\"-k\", \"-d\", \"1\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n   294→      stdin: null\n   295→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   296→    normalization: none\n   297→    expected:\n   298→      exit_code: 0\n   299→      stdout_structure: lines for immediate subdirectories and the root; no deeper entries\n   300→      stderr: \"\"\n   301→    traces:\n   302→      - prd009-du R2.4\n   303→\n   304→  - name: du_grand_total\n   305→    description: -c prints a grand total \"total\" line after all arguments.\n   306→    inputs:\n   307→      args: [\"-ck\", \"testdata/du-fixture/subdir1\", \"testdata/du-fixture/subdir2\"]\n   308→      stdin: null\n   309→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   310→    normalization: none\n   311→    expected:\n   312→      exit_code: 0\n   313→      stdout_structure: per-argument lines followed by a \"SIZE\\ttotal\" line\n   314→      stderr: \"\"\n   315→    traces:\n   316→      - prd009-du R2.7\n   317→\n   318→  - name: du_hard_link_dedup\n   319→    description: 'A file hard-linked into two directories is counted only once. Setup: create testdata/du-hardlink-fixture/ with dir_a/shared.txt (a regular file) and dir_b/shared.txt (hard link to dir_a/shared.txt, same inode). The hard link is created at test time via os.Link.'\n   320→    inputs:\n   321→      args: [\"-k\", \"testdata/du-hardlink-fixture/\"]\n   322→      stdin: null\n   323→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   324→    normalization: none\n   325→    expected:\n   326→      exit_code: 0\n   327→      stdout_structure: total for the root counts shared.txt blocks once, not twice\n   328→      stderr: \"\"\n   329→    traces:\n   330→      - prd009-du R3.1\n   331→      - prd009-du R3.2\n   332→      - prd009-du R3.3\n   333→\n   334→  - name: du_apparent_size\n   335→    description: --apparent-size reports st_size instead of st_blocks.\n   336→    inputs:\n   337→      args: [\"--apparent-size\", \"-k\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n   338→      stdin: null\n   339→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   340→    normalization: none\n   341→    expected:\n   342→      exit_code: 0\n   343→      stdout_structure: sizes based on file content length, not block allocation\n   344→      stderr: \"\"\n   345→    traces:\n   346→      - prd009-du R2.8\n   347→\n   348→  - name: du_kilobyte_units\n   349→    description: -k reports in 1024-byte blocks (default, accepted without error).\n   350→    inputs:\n   351→      args: [\"-k\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n   352→      stdin: null\n   353→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   354→    normalization: none\n   355→    expected:\n   356→      exit_code: 0\n   357→      stdout_structure: identical to default_recursive (1K is the default)\n   358→      stderr: \"\"\n   359→    traces:\n   360→      - prd009-du R2.5\n   361→\n   362→  - name: du_megabyte_units\n   363→    description: -m reports in 1048576-byte (1M) blocks.\n   364→    inputs:\n   365→      args: [\"-m\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n   366→      stdin: null\n   367→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   368→    normalization: none\n   369→    expected:\n   370→      exit_code: 0\n   371→      stdout_structure: sizes in megabyte units, smaller values show as 1 (rounded up)\n   372→      stderr: \"\"\n   373→    traces:\n   374→      - prd009-du R2.6\n   375→\n   376→  - name: du_missing_path\n   377→    description: Non-existent argument prints error to stderr, exits 1.\n   378→    inputs:\n   379→      args: [\"-k\", \"nonexistent_dir\"]\n   380→      stdin: null\n   381→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   382→    normalization: none\n   383→    expected:\n   384→      exit_code: 1\n   385→      stderr_contains: \"nonexistent_dir\"\n   386→    traces:\n   387→      - prd009-du R4.2\n   388→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rr3Nc2sNzdyNsNfUbKv85p","session_id":"f6586651-9e84-4147-a394-d5fc5f9feda5","uuid":"286edce6-4530-4b19-9118-0180d6d0e966"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01911wui8yUPYkWWwimNM1bu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011iM1qMUbFiGTiY413svGr1","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/generation-2026-02-27-21-48-32-21v/docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml","limit":150},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5379,"cache_read_input_tokens":35711,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5379},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rr3Nc2sNzdyNsNfUbKv85p","session_id":"f6586651-9e84-4147-a394-d5fc5f9feda5","uuid":"98ed5949-63b2-4c02-a633-3b9d42873e48"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011iM1qMUbFiGTiY413svGr1","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: go-unix-utils\n     2→title: \"go-unix-utils Architecture\"\n     3→\n     4→overview:\n     5→  summary: |\n     6→    go-unix-utils is a pipeline from C-source-derived specifications to verified Go\n     7→    binaries. Each utility follows the same four-stage flow: extract, specify, synthesize,\n     8→    verify. The synthesis stage is driven by mage-claude-orchestrator, an automated code\n     9→    generation system. Specification development is human-guided. A shared pkg/ library\n    10→    accumulates common logic as utilities are added.\n    11→  lifecycle: |\n    12→    For each utility a human operator clones the C source repository, analyzes flags and\n    13→    edge cases, and uses the make-work and do-work Claude Code skills to produce two\n    14→    specification artifacts: a PRD (numbered requirements and acceptance criteria covering\n    15→    all flags, exit codes, and stream behaviors) and a use case (concrete end-to-end\n    16→    execution path through the system). The PRD is the primary input to code generation.\n    17→    Once the spec artifacts are complete, the human invokes the mage-claude-orchestrator\n    18→    via mage targets; the orchestrator drives a Claude agent to generate Go code in\n    19→    cmd/<utility>/ and runs the differential testing harness. If tests fail, the operator\n    20→    refines the PRD and the orchestrator re-generates.\n    21→\n    22→    Shared library components (pkg/sys, pkg/format, pkg/testutils) may also have PRDs\n    23→    when their requirements are non-trivial and span multiple utilities.\n    24→  coordination_pattern: |\n    25→    The human operator owns the specification phase. The mage-claude-orchestrator owns\n    26→    the synthesis and verification phases. Mage targets (magefiles/orchestrator.go)\n    27→    expose the boundary between them: the operator calls mage targets to hand off to\n    28→    the orchestrator after the spec is ready. The differential testing harness in\n    29→    pkg/testutils/ is the shared acceptance criterion for both phases.\n    30→\n    31→interfaces:\n    32→  - name: Data Structures\n    33→    summary: |\n    34→      Specification artifacts and runtime data structures used across the pipeline.\n    35→    data_structures:\n    36→      - \"PRD (prd[NNN]-<utility>.yaml): per-utility product requirements document with numbered goals, requirements, and acceptance criteria.\"\n    37→      - \"Use case (rel[NN].[N]-uc[NNN]-<utility>.yaml): per-utility use case describing a concrete end-to-end execution path through the system.\"\n    38→      - \"DiffTest: Go struct in pkg/testutils/ defining a single differential test case with fields for input arguments, stdin, environment, expected exit code, and expected output.\"\n    39→      - \"configuration.yaml: orchestrator configuration file at the project root consumed by magefiles/ to configure build, analysis, and generation targets.\"\n    40→    operations:\n    41→      - \"mage build: compiles all cmd/ binaries to bin/.\"\n    42→      - \"mage lint: runs golangci-lint on all Go source under cmd/ and pkg/.\"\n    43→      - \"mage stats:loc: prints Go lines of code (production and test) and documentation word counts.\"\n    44→      - \"mage analyze: runs cross-artifact consistency checks on docs/ (PRDs, use cases, test suites, roadmap).\"\n    45→      - \"go test ./...: runs all tests including differential tests in each cmd/ package.\"\n    46→  - name: Events\n    47→    summary: |\n    48→      Observable events emitted by the system during operation.\n    49→    operations:\n    50→      - \"Differential test failure: go test reports the divergence with the input that triggered it, the expected output (reference binary), and the actual output (Go binary).\"\n    51→\n    52→components:\n    53→  - name: Human Operator\n    54→    responsibility: |\n    55→      Guides specification development for each utility. Clones the C source, analyzes\n    56→      flags and edge cases, and uses the make-work and do-work Claude Code skills to\n    57→      produce a PRD and a use case. Decides when the spec artifacts are complete enough\n    58→      to hand off to the orchestrator. Refines PRDs when orchestrator-generated code\n    59→      fails differential tests. Also authors PRDs for shared pkg/ components when their\n    60→      requirements warrant it.\n    61→    capabilities:\n    62→      - make-work skill breaks a utility into specification issues\n    63→      - do-work skill works through individual specification issues\n    64→      - C source analysis via cloned coreutils/moreutils/grep/findutils repositories\n    65→    references:\n    66→      - .claude/commands/\n    67→\n    68→  - name: Specification Repository\n    69→    responsibility: |\n    70→      Holds the formal per-utility PRDs and use cases alongside this documentation suite.\n    71→      Serves as the source of truth for synthesis and verification. Shared library\n    72→      components (pkg/) may also have PRDs.\n    73→    capabilities:\n    74→      - One PRD per utility under docs/specs/product-requirements/ (plus PRDs for shared pkg/ components as needed)\n    75→      - One use case per utility under docs/specs/use-cases/\n    76→      - VISION.yaml and ARCHITECTURE.yaml project-level docs\n    77→      - Test suites under docs/specs/test-suites/\n    78→    references:\n    79→      - docs/\n    80→\n    81→  - name: cmd/\n    82→    responsibility: |\n    83→      Holds the Go implementation of each utility. Each sub-package compiles to a\n    84→      standalone binary and contains its differential tests alongside the implementation.\n    85→      cmd/ grows as utilities are implemented following road-map.yaml. The full catalog\n    86→      of 123 target utilities (coreutils, moreutils, grep, findutils) is in\n    87→      docs/utilities.yaml; stdbuf is the only utility in those repos that is explicitly\n    88→      excluded (LD_PRELOAD injection not possible in pure Go).\n    89→    capabilities:\n    90→      - One package per utility, named cmd/<utility>/\n    91→      - Each package contains main.go (implementation) and <utility>_test.go (differential tests)\n    92→      - Active roadmap in road-map.yaml for current release and use case status\n    93→      - Full catalog in docs/utilities.yaml for difficulty, memory model, and implementation profile of each utility\n    94→    references:\n    95→      - cmd/\n    96→\n    97→  - name: pkg/sys/\n    98→    responsibility: |\n    99→      Wraps Darwin and Linux syscalls and signal handling. Provides a stable interface\n   100→      that cmd/ packages use to avoid platform-specific code in utility implementations.\n   101→      Only syscalls that have platform divergence between Darwin and Linux, or that Go's\n   102→      standard library does not expose cleanly, belong here.\n   103→    capabilities:\n   104→      - Terminal size queries (TIOCGWINSZ ioctl)\n   105→      - Signal handling (SIGPIPE, SIGHUP, SIGWINCH)\n   106→      - File metadata (stat, lstat; abstracts st_mtimespec/st_mtim and st_blocks divergence)\n   107→      - Process group management (setpgid, killpg) for timeout and xargs -P\n   108→      - Process priority (setpriority) for nice and renice\n   109→    references:\n   110→      - pkg/sys/\n   111→\n   112→  - name: pkg/format/\n   113→    responsibility: |\n   114→      Provides output formatting shared across utilities including table alignment,\n   115→      ANSI color output, and human-readable unit conversion (bytes to K/M/G).\n   116→    capabilities:\n   117→      - Column alignment for tabular output (ls -l style)\n   118→      - ANSI color codes for file types and permissions\n   119→      - Human-readable size formatting\n   120→    references:\n   121→      - pkg/format/\n   122→\n   123→  - name: pkg/testutils/\n   124→    responsibility: |\n   125→      The differential testing harness. Executes a Go binary and a reference GNU binary\n   126→      with the same inputs and compares stdout, stderr, and exit code byte-for-byte or\n   127→      with configured normalization.\n   128→    capabilities:\n   129→      - Execute two binaries with identical stdin, arguments, and environment\n   130→      - Compare stdout, stderr, and exit code\n   131→      - Report divergence with the input, expected output, and actual output\n   132→      - Support normalization hooks for known acceptable differences (e.g., timestamps)\n   133→    references:\n   134→      - pkg/testutils/\n   135→\n   136→  - name: magefiles/\n   137→    responsibility: |\n   138→      Mage build targets for the project. Wraps build, lint, test, stats, and analyze\n   139→      operations. Delegates to the mage-claude-orchestrator library, which drives Claude\n   140→      agents for code generation. This is the boundary between the human-guided spec\n   141→      phase and the automated synthesis phase.\n   142→    capabilities:\n   143→      - mage build compiles all binaries\n   144→      - mage lint runs golangci-lint\n   145→      - mage stats:loc prints LOC and doc word counts\n   146→      - mage analyze runs cross-artifact consistency checks\n   147→      - mage init initializes project (beads)\n   148→      - mage credentials extracts Claude credentials from macOS Keychain\n   149→      - mage cobbler:measure and mage cobbler:stitch run the orchestrator generation cycle\n   150→    references:"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rr3Nc2sNzdyNsNfUbKv85p","session_id":"f6586651-9e84-4147-a394-d5fc5f9feda5","uuid":"04ab38e1-3fda-495d-ae0e-2eb33c71dcfd"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rr3Nc2sNzdyNsNfUbKv85p","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the project. Let me create a final summary document:\n\n## Project Structure Summary\n\nThis is **go-unix-utils**, a specification-driven code generation project that produces Go implementations of 123 Unix utilities (from coreutils, moreutils, grep, findutils) verified against GNU reference binaries via differential testing.\n\n### Key Characteristics\n\n**Phase**: Specification-complete, code generation pipeline ready\n- Repository currently contains only specifications and documentation (code generation is delegated to the mage-claude-orchestrator)\n- No Go source code exists yet in cmd/ or pkg/\n- Binary artifacts exist in the root (cat, sponge, ts, wc - these are built binaries from previous generation runs)\n\n### Top-Level Directory Structure\n\n```\n/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/generation-2026-02-27-21-48-32-21v/\n├── .beads/                          # Cobbler (AI orchestrator) state directory\n├── .secrets/                        # Credentials storage\n├── .git                             # Worktree git reference\n├── .gitignore, .gitattributes      # Git configuration\n├── LICENSE                          # Project license\n├── README.md                        # Project overview\n├── configuration.yaml               # Orchestrator configuration\n├── cat, sponge, ts, wc             # Compiled binaries from previous generation runs\n├── docs/                            # Complete specification suite\n├── magefiles/                       # Build orchestration (mage build targets)\n└── (No pkg/ directory yet - will be created during generation)\n```\n\n### Core Configuration (configuration.yaml)\n\n- **Module Path**: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`\n- **Binary Directory**: `bin/`\n- **Source Directories**: `pkg`, `cmd` (to be generated)\n- **Orchestrator**: Configured for Claude-based code generation with specific constitution files for planning, execution, design, and Go style\n\n### Documentation Structure (docs/)\n\n```\ndocs/\n├── VISION.yaml                     # Project goals, risks, boundaries\n├── ARCHITECTURE.yaml               # Components, design decisions, tech choices\n├── SPECIFICATIONS.yaml             # Index of all PRDs, use cases, test suites\n├── utilities.yaml                  # Complete catalog of 123 target utilities\n├── road-map.yaml                   # Release schedule and status\n├── constitutions/                  # AI generation guidelines (planning, execution, design, go-style)\n├── engineering/                    # Engineering docs and generation run results (eng01-eng12)\n├── prompts/                        # measure.yaml, stitch.yaml (orchestrator prompts)\n└── specs/\n    ├── product-requirements/       # 10 PRDs (7 utilities + 3 shared components)\n    ├── use-cases/                  # 7 use cases (rel01.0-rel02.1)\n    └── test-suites/               # 4 test suites (rel01.0-rel02.1)\n```\n\n### Product Requirements Documents (10 Total)\n\n**Shared Components (3 PRDs)**:\n1. **prd001-testutils.yaml** - Differential testing harness (`pkg/testutils/`)\n   - DiffTest struct for test case definition\n   - RunDiffTests() function to execute Go and GNU binaries side-by-side\n   - Normalization hooks for non-deterministic output (timestamps)\n   - File-state comparison for utilities like sponge, cp\n\n2. **prd002-sys.yaml** - Syscall abstractions (`pkg/sys/`)\n   - TerminalWidth(), IsTerminal() - TTY/terminal width detection\n   - Stat(), Lstat() - Extended file metadata (nlink, uid, gid, rdev, blocks, ino, dev)\n   - FileInfo struct with 11 fields (Mode, Size, Nlink, Uid, Gid, Rdev, Dev, Ino, Blocks, Blksize, ModTime, Sys)\n   - InstallSIGPIPEHandler() - Graceful broken-pipe handling\n   - OnTerminalResize() - SIGWINCH callback registration\n\n3. **prd003-format.yaml** - Output formatting (`pkg/format/`)\n   - Columns() - Multi-column layout computation\n   - PadLeft(), PadRight() - Field alignment\n   - FileTypeColor() - ANSI color codes for file types\n   - HumanSize() - Binary/SI unit conversion (bytes → K/M/G/T/P/E)\n\n**Utilities (7 PRDs)**:\n1. **prd004-ts.yaml** - timestamp utility (rel01.0)\n2. **prd005-wc.yaml** - word/line/byte count (rel01.1)\n3. **prd006-cat.yaml** - concatenate files (rel01.1)\n4. **prd007-sponge.yaml** - soak up stdin to file (rel01.1)\n5. **prd008-ls.yaml** - directory listing **[FOCUS AREA]** (rel02.0)\n6. **prd009-du.yaml** - disk usage (rel02.0)\n7. **prd010-ls-extended.yaml** - ls extended flags (rel02.1, deferred)\n\n### Release Structure\n\n**rel01.0** (ts)\n- 1 utility: ts\n- 1 use case, 1 test suite\n\n**rel01.1** (wc, cat, sponge)\n- 3 utilities: wc, cat, sponge\n- 3 use cases, 1 test suite\n\n**rel02.0** (ls core, du) **[CURRENT SCOPE]**\n- 2 utilities: ls (core flags), du\n- 2 use cases, 1 test suite (test-rel02.0.yaml)\n\n**rel02.1** (ls extended)\n- 1 utility: ls (extended flags like -C, -x, -t, -S, -r, -R, -F)\n- 1 use case, 1 test suite\n\n### ls Command Specification (prd008-ls.yaml) - Core Focus\n\n**Scope**: Core flags for rel02.0\n\n**In-scope flags**:\n- Default (multi-column on TTY, single-column on pipe)\n- `-1` - Force single-column\n- `-l` - Long format (permissions, nlink, owner, group, size, mtime, name)\n- `-a` - Show all (including . and ..)\n- `-A` - Almost all (dotfiles except . and ..)\n- `-d` - List directory itself, not contents\n- `-h` - Human-readable sizes (with -l only)\n- `--color=[always|auto|never]` - ANSI colorization\n- `-w WIDTH` - Terminal width override\n\n**Out-of-scope for rel02.0**:\n- `-C` (force multi-column), `-x` (across sort), `-t` (time sort), `-S` (size sort), `-r` (reverse), `-U`, `-v`, `-i` (inode), `-s` (block size), `-n` (numeric IDs), `-R` (recursive), `-F` (classify)\n- `--hyperlink`, `--dired`, `-Z` (SELinux), `--quoting-style`, `--block-size` (beyond -h), `LS_COLORS` parsing, ACL display\n\n**Key Requirements**:\n- Terminal width detection for multi-column layout (via pkg/sys.TerminalWidth())\n- Extended file metadata (via pkg/sys.Stat/Lstat)\n- Column alignment (via pkg/format.Columns)\n- Permission string formatting (10-char: type + 3×(rwx) with setuid/setgid/sticky)\n- Owner/group name resolution (os/user.LookupId/LookupGroupId)\n- Mtime formatting (\"Jan _2 15:04\" if <6 months, else \"Jan _2  2006\")\n- Block count display (\"total N\" where N = sum(Blocks)/2)\n- Symlink display (\"name -> target\")\n- Color output (GNU LS_COLORS defaults)\n- Human-readable sizes (binary 1024-based: K/M/G/T/P/E)\n- Exit codes: 0 (success), 1 (minor error: access denied), 2 (serious: bad option)\n- Signal handling: SIGPIPE (exit cleanly), SIGWINCH (re-query width on terminal resize)\n- C locale sorting (LC_COLLATE=C)\n\n### Use Case (rel02.0-uc001-ls.yaml)\n\n**Test Fixture**: `testdata/ls-fixture/`\n- Regular files of known sizes\n- Subdirectory\n- Dotfiles (e.g., .hidden)\n- Symbolic link\n- Files with known permissions\n\n**Differential Testing Approach**:\n1. Run both `./bin/ls` (Go) and `gls` (GNU reference via Homebrew) with same args/env\n2. Apply LsNormalizer to replace mtime column with placeholder (wall-clock independent)\n3. Compare normalized outputs byte-for-byte\n4. Use `LC_ALL=C` and `--color=never` to eliminate variance\n\n**Test Suite** (test-rel02.0.yaml):\n18 ls test cases covering:\n- Default single-column (redirected)\n- Multi-column with -C and -w\n- Single-column with -1\n- Long format (-l, -lh, with symlinks)\n- Filter flags (-a, -A, -d)\n- Color modes (--color=never, --color=always, auto detection)\n- Error handling (missing files → exit 1, bad options → exit 2)\n\n### Shared Components Details\n\n**pkg/testutils** (prd001-testutils.yaml):\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n    Name string\n    Args []string\n    Stdin []byte          // nil = EOF, []byte{} = open+close\n    Env []string          // nil = inherit, non-nil = override\n    ExitCode int\n    Normalize []func([]byte) []byte\n    ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte\n}\n\nfunc RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)\n```\n\n**pkg/sys** (prd002-sys.yaml):\n```go\ntype FileInfo struct {\n    Mode os.FileMode\n    Size int64\n    Nlink uint64\n    Uid uint32\n    Gid uint32\n    Rdev uint64\n    Dev uint64\n    Ino uint64\n    Blocks int64       // st_blocks / 2 for 1K blocks\n    Blksize int64\n    ModTime time.Time\n    Sys os.FileInfo\n}\n\nfunc TerminalWidth() (int, error)\nfunc IsTerminal(w io.Writer) bool\nfunc Stat(path string) (*FileInfo, error)\nfunc Lstat(path string) (*FileInfo, error)\nfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\nfunc OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int))\n```\n\n**pkg/format** (prd003-format.yaml):\n```go\nfunc Columns(entries []string, termWidth int) [][]string\nfunc PadLeft(s string, width int) string\nfunc PadRight(s string, width int) string\nfunc FileTypeColor(mode os.FileMode) string\nfunc Reset() string\nfunc ColorEnabled(w io.Writer) bool\nfunc HumanSize(bytes int64, opts HumanSizeOpts) string\n\ntype HumanSizeOpts struct {\n    Binary bool  // true = 1024-based (default), false = 1000-based (SI)\n}\n```\n\n### Build and Test Infrastructure\n\n- **Magefiles**: `magefiles/orchestrator.go` - Integration with mage-claude-orchestrator\n- **Mage Targets**:\n  - `mage build` - Compile all binaries to bin/\n  - `mage lint` - Run golangci-lint\n  - `mage test` - Run all tests including differential tests\n  - `mage analyze` - Cross-artifact consistency checks\n  - `mage stats:loc` - Lines of code + documentation word counts\n  - `mage cobbler:measure` - Measure phase of orchestrator\n  - `mage cobbler:stitch` - Stitch (code generation) phase\n\n### Previous Generation Runs\n\nThe repo includes documentation of 6 completed generation runs (eng04-eng12):\n- First run: 4,586 lines of Go across 22 files in 16 measure+stitch cycles\n- Produced: 2,842 production lines + 1,744 test lines\n- Available at v1.YYYYMMDD.N tags\n- Current working branch is specification-only (v0 state)\n\n### Next Steps for Implementation\n\nThe `ls` implementation needs to create:\n\n1. **pkg/sys/** package with:\n   - TerminalWidth() using TIOCGWINSZ ioctl\n   - IsTerminal() TTY detection\n   - Stat/Lstat with extended FileInfo struct\n   - InstallSIGPIPEHandler and OnTerminalResize\n\n2. **pkg/format/** package with:\n   - Columns() for multi-column layout\n   - Padding functions\n   - FileTypeColor() for ANSI codes\n   - HumanSize() for unit conversion\n\n3. **pkg/testutils/** package with:\n   - DiffTest struct\n   - RunDiffTests() harness\n   - LsNormalizer for timestamp replacement\n\n4. **cmd/ls/** package with:\n   - main.go implementing the ls command\n   - ls_test.go with differential test cases\n   - Comprehensive flag parsing and formatting logic\n\nAll file paths mentioned are absolute paths within the worktree root at:\n`/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/generation-2026-02-27-21-48-32-21v/`"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a4de4ecb908b4a7d7 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 47282\ntool_uses: 23\nduration_ms: 61815</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6586651-9e84-4147-a394-d5fc5f9feda5","uuid":"0aabc438-34e2-44ac-9c8e-2c7cca35c889","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand the current project structure. Please:\n1. Read go.mod if it exists at the project root\n2. Check if pkg/sys/ directory exists and read any .go files in it\n3. Check if pkg/format/ directory exists and read any .go files in it  \n4. Check if pkg/testutils/ directory exists and read any .go files in it\n5. Read configuration.yaml\n6. List the top-level directory contents with `ls -la`\n7. Check if there are any Go source files anywhere: glob for **/*.go\n8. Check if there's a bin/ directory\n