n C locale. I need to verify the sorting behavior is working correctly after adding entries, and double-check the numeric formatting for UIDs and GIDs matches what gls produces. The block count column width should be fine since the values are small, but I should verify gls's padding behavior to ensure the output aligns properly.\n\nSince gls isn't available to test against, I'll proceed with my implementation and trust it matches the spec, fixing any discrepancies if they come up later. I also need to make sure the -F classification indicator appears after the ANSI color reset sequence when colors are enabled, per the requirements—currently my code adds the indicator outside the color tags, which is correct, but I'm noticing a potential bug in how the name is being handled when color is enabled.\n\nActually, looking at it more carefully, the implementation is correct: the indicator gets appended after the reset sequence, so it displays in the default color rather than inheriting the file's color. I'm verifying this works properly for directories, executables, and other file types. Now I need to check how symlink indicators behave in long format output.\n\nWriting symlink handling code...\n\nI'm confident the implementation matches GNU ls behavior. Now I should add structural tests to cover these cases and then finalize the code, though I'm also thinking through potential issues with how the test environment will handle both binaries pointing at the same fixture directory. the same files, they'll see the same inodes. So the differential test should pass. Both binaries use st_blocks from stat, so the block counts should agree, and since they compute the total the same way, those should match too. For the -n flag, they'll show the same UID/GID, and for -F, the file indicators will be consistent since they're based on the same file modes. I'm confident this implementation is solid, so let me add some structural tests and clean things up. Actually, I should manually test