{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01R28dQKjcgiGE4sZto4cS4g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Implementation complete. Here's a summary of what was created:\n\n**Files created:**\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `go.mod` | Go module definition with `golang.org/x/sys` dependency |\n| `pkg/sys/sys.go` | Common types: `FileInfo` struct, `IsTerminal()` |\n| `pkg/sys/sys_linux.go` | Linux impl: `Stat`, `Lstat`, `TerminalWidth`, `InstallSIGPIPEHandler`, `OnTerminalResize` |\n| `pkg/testutils/testutils.go` | Differential testing harness: `DiffTest`, `RunDiffTests`, normalizers |\n| `cmd/ls/main.go` | ls command with core flags + extended flags `-i`, `-s`, `-n`, `-F` |\n| `cmd/ls/ls_test.go` | Differential tests (skip when gls unavailable) + structural tests |\n\n**Implemented requirements (prd010-ls-extended):**\n\n- **R3.1 (-i)**: Prepends right-aligned inode number (`sys.FileInfo.Ino`) to each entry\n- **R3.2 (-s)**: Prepends right-aligned 1K block count (`fi.Blocks/2`); shows \"total\" line\n- **R3.4 (-n)**: Implies `-l`; displays numeric UID/GID via `strconv.FormatUint`\n- **R3.5**: When `-i` and `-s` combined, inode first, then block count, then entry\n- **R4.1 (-F)**: Appends type indicators: `/` dir, `*` exec, `@` symlink, `|` FIFO, `=` socket\n- **R4.3**: Indicator printed after ANSI reset so it's not colorized\n- **R6.1**: `-n` implies `-l`\n- **R6.5**: `-s -h` uses binary humanSize algorithm inlined in cmd/ls\n\n**Verification results:**\n- `go build ./cmd/ls/` — compiles cleanly\n- `golangci-lint run ./...` — 0 issues\n- `go test ./...` — all 7 structural tests PASS; 8 differential tests SKIP (gls not available)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":674,"cache_read_input_tokens":138350,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":674},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo